{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.InvMonomialDet","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.InvMonomialDet","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Determinant.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Equiv.Basic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.det_of_inv_monomial_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.det_of_inv_monomial_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/InvMonomialDet.lean#L62-L70","doc":"Over a field such a determinant vanishes exactly when one of the entries\ndoes — the sign is a unit and contributes nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.det_of_inv_monomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.det_of_inv_monomial","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/InvMonomialDet.lean#L54-L60","doc":"**The inversion case.**  On a finite group, a matrix whose only nonzero\nentries sit at `(v, v⁻¹)` has determinant `sign(inv) · ∏ f`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.det_of_graph_monomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.det_of_graph_monomial","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/InvMonomialDet.lean#L37-L52","doc":"**A matrix supported on the graph of `σ` is `sign σ` times the product of\nits nonzero entries.**\n\n`M v w = f v` when `w = σ v` and `0` otherwise; it is `diagonal f` with its\ncolumns permuted, which is why `Matrix.det_permute'` closes it. ","signatureChunk":0}]}